<!--
  Amazing Grace
  Tune "New Britain" (American, 1829), words by John Newton (1779). Public domain.
  C major, 3/4, quarter = 80, pickup + 16 bars (36 s). Right hand: the melody, G3-G4.
  "me" and "see" are held for five beats, as in the hymnals.
  Left hand: roots C3 F3 G3, one per bar. Every note is in C3-B4.

  bar | right hand  | left hand | words
    0 | G3          | -         | A-
    1 | C4 E4 C4    | C3        | -ma-zing
    2 | E4 D4       | C3        | grace, how
    3 | C4 A3       | F3        | sweet the
    4 | G3 G3       | C3        | sound that
    5 | C4 E4 C4    | C3        | saved a
    6 | E4 D4       | C3        | wretch like
    7 | G4          | G3        | me!
    8 | (G4) E4     | G3        | I
    9 | G4 E4 G4 E4 | C3        | once was
   10 | C4 G3       | C3        | lost, but
   11 | A3 C4 C4 A3 | F3        | now am
   12 | G3 G3       | C3        | found, was
   13 | C4 E4 C4    | C3        | blind, but
   14 | E4 D4       | G3        | now I
   15 | C4          | C3        | see.
   16 | (C4)        | (C3)      |
-->
